{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/287726-ornery-6000-xp-lunar-exalt-when-isn-t-it-fun","id":287726,"title":"Ornery 6000 xp Lunar exalt, when isn't it fun?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-20T09:31:09-07:00","id":287726,"title":"Ornery 6000 xp Lunar exalt, when isn't it fun?","content":"I found my self thinking a few weeks ago that when I'm in the proper mood (i.e. surly, not feeling up to challenges that test me) that a Ornery 6000 xp lunar exalted would be the ideal character to play in an RPG. The surprising part was that it wasn't just Exalted where my grumpy longing to kick ass self wanted to play this character but in fact, as near as I could tell, every RPG game ever.<br /> <br /> Shadowrun,<br /> <br /> D&amp;D,<br /> <br /> all those hundreds of just like D&amp;D but different games<br /> <br /> any World of darkness game,<br /> <br /> legend of the five rings (oh hell yes!)<br /> <br /> any super hero game<br /> <br /> Dogs in the Vineyard<br /> <br /> Pantheon (yes I know that it would be impossible and I'd worse than loose I'd destroy the game- that kind of makes me want to play it more)<br /> <br /> Adventures of Baron von Munchausen (a drinking game of competitive lying dressed up as an rpg)<br /> <br /> Rune<br /> <br /> Paranoia<br /> <br /> Toon<br /> <br /> Star Trek (&quot;Prime directive shrime directive - I'm going to eat his heart&quot;)<br /> <br /> Star wars<br /> <br /> Teenagers from outer space<br /> <br /> Call of Cuthullu<br /> <br /> Amber<br /> <br /> Ars Magica<br /> <br /> So if I'm an ill tempered grump can you think of an RPG where it wouldn't be cathartic to play a preposterously powerful Lunar exalted who is an ill tempered grump<br /> <br /> (Noblis?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":872,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","user":"Apromor","date":". 10-20-2014, 12:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T09:39:44-07:00","id":287752,"title":"","content":"Make sure to partner with a Solar who isn't such a grump.<br /> <br /> Then when that Solar dies, seek out their next reincarnation and partner with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T10:24:30-07:00","id":287814,"title":"","content":"6000 XP means that the character and the ST who feels like handling him would be doing actual storytelling. Rolls are obviated by the character having that much XP under his belt. It can be done, but it takes a lot of effort on everyone's parts.<br /> Also, no other games could handle someone at that level of power unless you want to move to the cosmic level of superhero games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T13:00:31-07:00","id":287949,"title":"","content":"Warhammer 40K ought to be hilarious. Heal up the golden guy for shits and giggles. Slap the Warp into submission on a bet. Get into an eating contest with the Tyranids. Adopt the Orks - lovable scamps that they are - when they declare you to be their previously-unknown third god of Orkyness.<br /> <br /> Do a guest appearance in Call of Cthulhu; have it turn out that you're the Great Old One everyone was worrying about.<br /> <br /> I don't know the answer to the OP's premiss, mostly because I can't think of a reason why it wouldn't be immensely cathartic to play a crazy powerful Elder Lunar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Aretii: &quot;As one of the players described it, 'After initiation, it was actually a relief seeing who had eyepatches or bandaged hands - you know what <i>they</i> sacrificed, instead of wondering what bits people cut out of their own souls to gain power.'&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/578-lord-sia","name":"Lord Sia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T17:16:56-07:00","id":288082,"title":"","content":"...<i>how </i>much xp? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Yeah, I can't really think if a setting he couldn't wreck, either. Maybe Scion... maybe. The high-end characters there have powers that basically outright say &quot;narrate how you win this scene,&quot; but a Lunar THAT high up could probably outlast the scene and then still eat them. I can't really think of any threat in any game that he couldn't solo with that kind of power... shit, about 9/10 of his charms could be Essence 10 if he wanted...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T19:36:46-07:00","id":288164,"title":"","content":"When it's a 1e or 2e Lunar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T20:46:33-07:00","id":288215,"title":"","content":"((trolling))<br /> <br /> I don't know. In most D&amp;D editions, 6000 xp isn't much. I think at best that's about level 4, isn't it?<br /> <br /> ((/trolling))","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T06:47:04-07:00","id":288497,"title":"","content":"Ye tiny gods. Um...huh.<br /> <br /> A setting that playing a stupidly powerful shapeshifter loaded with 'screw you' abilities wouldn't be cathartic to play in....<br /> <br /> Even in a setting where combat isn't the focus, it wouldn't matter. You can break out the <a href=\"http://rollperception.com/viewtopic.php?f=4&amp;t=281\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Kitty Revolution</a> at fairly low XP levels, and completely upend most settings by co-opting control of all the NPCs. And now that you can control the NPCs, you can make the setting as entertaining as you'd like.<br /> <br /> A Lunar would straight up rock at Shadowrun, even at lower level. And at 6K XP, you'd probably have Heart's Blood from one of the Great Dragons by the end of the first session, and quietly file it away under 'less powerful forms.'<br /> <br /> Star Wars, you'd overthrow or rule the Galactic Empire in a weekend.<br /> <br /> Firefly: pretty much the same story against the Alliance.<br /> <br /> It is theoretically possible that The Dresden Files RPG might be able to produce some critters in your weight class if your GM is creative enough...but Perfects still unbalance things ridiculously. And the fact that you have enough Essence to spam Perfects every single time something attacks<br /> <br /> As others have mentioned, C'thulu would probably end up as your spiffy new pet...or you'd eat it.<br /> <br /> Heck, even the My Little Pony RPG could be immensely cathartic, depending on how dark of a place you wanted to take that story. (New Motivation: Heart's Blood of ALL the Alicorns!)<br /> <br /> The Game That Must Not Be Named would be...weird to say the least. But you'd win, with ease. (and hopefully you'd bring about the apocalypse)<br /> <br /> Executive Decision probably wouldn't be quite as cathartic...as it is basically a game about convincing the President of the US to act a certain way during a crisis. Sure, you'd win, with zero trouble...but that still sounds boring as crap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3937,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3937-guildsbounty","user":"guildsbounty","date":". 10-21-2014, 09:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3937-guildsbounty","name":"guildsbounty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T07:07:44-07:00","id":288503,"title":"","content":"do lunars even have 6k xp worth of charms?<br /> as someone who plays a 1k+ xp alchemical colossus, you can be stupid good at everything with maybe 2k xp","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Get that Lich some Zombies, Liches Love Zombies","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1913-katsutoshi","name":"Katsutoshi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1913_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T07:21:17-07:00","id":288516,"title":"","content":"No, Lunars do not have 6K XP worth of charms. A vast swath of their charms would be homebrewed, likely Essence 10. The charm descriptions would probably read something like &quot;The Lunar Eats You. It is a Perfect Attack. Because F___ You.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3937,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3937-guildsbounty","user":"guildsbounty","date":". 10-21-2014, 10:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3937-guildsbounty","name":"guildsbounty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T07:31:06-07:00","id":288522,"title":"","content":"Spending 6k XP does not necessitate spending 6k XP on Charms. And probably shouldn't, because then you'll be a guy with 6000 XP worth of Charms and crappy chargen levels of other stats.<br /> <br /> You're looking at several to raise your core and secondary Attributes to 10 and your tertiary ones above 5, and you'll want to, because dice caps. And probably some Abilities too, just for big passive dice pools.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guildsbounty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/287726-ornery-6000-xp-lunar-exalt-when-isn-t-it-fun?p=288516#post288516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, Lunars do not have 6K XP worth of charms. A vast swath of their charms would be homebrewed, likely Essence 10. The charm descriptions would probably read something like &quot;The Lunar Eats You. It is a Perfect Attack. Because F___ You.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>lol nah a perfect attack as Essence 10 would be a pretty pathetic Essence 10 Charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T13:38:52-07:00","id":288857,"title":"","content":"It boggles my mind when people talk about playing characters with 1000xp.<br /> <br /> Assuming people play on average once per week, with 52 weeks in a year and an average of 5xp per game session, it would take about 4 years of gameplay to reach that point. for a 6000xp character, it would take over 20 years to reach that level.<br /> <br /> Craziness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T14:21:41-07:00","id":288880,"title":"","content":"A 6k xp character would pretty much always be less fun than a character with far less xp, since that's so much xp that not only would you need a 200-page cheat sheet for their powers, but all their distinctiveness would have been annihilated in the course of finding things to spend XP on. At some point you'd be reduced to just taking ridiculous specialties for the hell of it.<br /> <br /> At this point you would really want to just be playing freeform with no specific set of capabilities for your character, and <i>even then</i> having a character that powerful would severely narrow the pool of stories you might want to tell. In general, becoming more powerful reduces the quality of Exalted games above a certain point, and this is way, way above that point.<br /> <br /> If all you want is to be <i>functionally omnipotent</i>, you would be better off just writing &quot;functionally omnipotent&quot; on your sheet and not pretending to use the system. But I can't imagine anybody <i>else</i> would want to play in the same group as a character whose concept is &quot;functionally omnipotent ill-tempered grump&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 10-21-2014, 05:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T15:28:37-07:00","id":288995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/287726-ornery-6000-xp-lunar-exalt-when-isn-t-it-fun?p=288880#post288880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If all you want is to be <i>functionally omnipotent</i>, you would be better off just writing &quot;functionally omnipotent&quot; on your sheet and not pretending to use the system. But I can't imagine anybody <i>else</i> would want to play in the same group as a character whose concept is &quot;functionally omnipotent ill-tempered grump&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly don't think even an essence 10 Lunar is functionally omnipotent. He's hella powerful, scary as shit of course, but he's not going to casually make the Imperium of Man and it's 250 billion star systems his bitch in and afternoon. Nor is he going to use a C'tan star god for a footstool or swat aside the platinum dragon-god Tiamat.<br /> <br /> He WILL be able to battle Tiamat or go on an epic quest to seal away the Nightbringer though, which is more than almost anyone ever can say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T17:01:31-07:00","id":289106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/287726-ornery-6000-xp-lunar-exalt-when-isn-t-it-fun?p=288995#post288995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I honestly don't think even an essence 10 Lunar is functionally omnipotent. He's hella powerful, scary as shit of course, but he's not going to casually make the Imperium of Man and it's 250 billion star systems his bitch in and afternoon. Nor is he going to use a C'tan star god for a footstool or swat aside the platinum dragon-god Tiamat.<br /> <br /> He WILL be able to battle Tiamat or go on an epic quest to seal away the Nightbringer though, which is more than almost anyone ever can say.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a &quot;sufficiently advanced technology&quot; issue. The ways in which a 6000 xp Lunar is not functionally omnipotent are sufficiently abstruse and complex that they aren't really worth simulating within the scope of the system. I mean, this character is probably going to have like 100 custom homebrewed Essence 6+ charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T23:38:02-07:00","id":289296,"title":"","content":"Guys. You guys. Guys. Hey, you guys.<br /> <br /> Shush with that talk, I wanna hear about whacky Lunar shenanigans. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T01:03:38-07:00","id":289328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/287726-ornery-6000-xp-lunar-exalt-when-isn-t-it-fun?p=289296#post289296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guys. You guys. Guys. Hey, you guys.<br /> <br /> Shush with that talk, I wanna hear about whacky Lunar shenanigans. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry. Ummm...well after defeating Tiamat the five headed chromatic dragon god-queen you could definitely take her heart's blood and become her, in whatever her base form is. Effectively inserting yourself into the pantheon of gods by succession.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T18:47:25-07:00","id":290197,"title":"","content":"Kay.<br /> <br /> <b>Bored Uber-Elder Lunar to-do list, sorted by setting!</b><br /> <br /> <b>DC Comics-verse</b><br /> Arm-wrestle Superman, Captain Marvel, Martian Manhunter, and Darkseid. All at once.<br /> Shifting contest with Plastic Man.<br /> Sample all the different forms of Kryptonite. Just in case.<br /> Kill Superboy Prime's punk-ass. I won't soil my form library with his crazy, he just needs to go.<br /> Threesome with Wonder Woman and Starfire.<br /> <br /> <b>Dresdenverse</b><br /> Cull the Outsiders to a manageable level. Might need to cull Winter too, now that they don't need as many soldiers.<br /> Fill in for Harry for a while so he can take some time to get his shit together re: friends and family.<br /> <br /> <b>Greek Mythology</b><br /> Father a new generation of gods upon Gaia.<br /> Become female, bear Zeus the son who will overthrow him.<br /> Convince the virgin goddesses to give it a try. &quot;Just once doesn't count, I won't tell...&quot;<br /> Lift the mountain off of Typhon and finish him off properly. By which I mean, take his Heart's Blood.<br /> <br /> <b>Honorverse</b><br /> Time to show those Mesan nutjobs what biological perfection <i>really </i>looks like.<br /> <br /> <b>Middle Earth</b><br /> Catch the Black Arrow in mid-flight, and make Smaug immortal. By which I mean, take his Heart's Blood.<br /> (Movie version of The Hobbit only) Slap that insufferable Mary Sue Legolas and his jerkass dad right out of the movie.<br /> Save the hobbits the trip by eating the One Ring. Volcano's got nothing on my stomach.<br /> <br /> <b>Star Wars</b><br /> Heart's Blood shopping list: the Death Star, that lava worm from the dying planet, those space-manta things that swim through hyperspace and poop gemstones*... ooh, Yuuzhan Vong Worldship!<br /> Yes, I said the Death Star. What, you can't turn into machines? Newb.<br /> Eat the Yuuzhan Vong. All of them.<br /> Do Zeltros. Yes, I mean it <i>exactly </i>that way.<br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">*Yes, these are actually a thing in the Star Wars EU.</span><br /> <br /> <b>Warhammer 40k</b><br /> Collect C'tan Heart's Blood.<br /> Heal the Emperor, and tell him not to fuck it up this time around.<br /> Rescue Isha from Nurgle.<br /> Single-handedly repopulate the Eldar. Yes, I mean it <i>exactly </i>that way.<br /> Gank the Chaos Gods.<br /> Eat a Hive-Fleet or two.<br /> Show the Kroot how it's done.<br /> <br /> <b>Zombie Apocalypse</b> (Any)<br /> Eat a zombie's brain, just for the irony.<br /> Add the contagion to my library.<br /> Take it to other universes to see if anyone actually gets it right on the first try.<br /> Wipe out the zombies, except for one continent from which I'll evacuate all the humans. That way, I have my own private zombie hunting preserve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/